BT 1 0 0 1 0 143.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The criminal procedural code decides who may stop a march, on what material, for how long, subject to) Tj T* (what review, and with what consequence for a person who does not comply. For more than a century this) Tj T* (was section 144 of the Code of Criminal Procedure. On 1 July 2024 the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita,) Tj T* (2023 replaced the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973, alongside the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 \(BNS\) and) Tj T* (the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023. The Bill was introduced in August 2023, referred to the) Tj T* (Parliamentary Standing Committee on Home Affairs, withdrawn and reintroduced in a revised form in) Tj T* (December 2023, passed by both Houses that month and notified in the Gazette after Presidential assent on) Tj T* (25 December 2023. The old Section 144 is now Section 163 of the new Sanhita, which is why a Delhi Police) Tj T* (order restricting gatherings around Parliament Street is now described as a Section 163 order and not a) Tj T* (Section 144 order.) Tj T* ET
