BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The Police Act, 1861 empowered the police to regulate the conduct of assemblies and processions in public) Tj T* (streets and to require licences for them. The Code of Criminal Procedure, as it developed under the Raj and) Tj T* (was consolidated in 1898, gave magistrates the power to issue urgent orders to prevent obstruction,) Tj T* (annoyance or disturbance of public tranquillity, which is the power that Indians came to know by the) Tj T* (number 144. Alongside these, the penal law criminalised unlawful assembly and rioting, and political speech) Tj T* (was policed through the offence of sedition and special statutes such as the Seditious Meetings Act, 1907) Tj T* (and the Prevention of Seditious Meetings Act, 1911. The Rowlatt Acts of 1919 extended preventive) Tj T* (detention and special tribunals into peacetime.) Tj T* ET
