q
1 1 1 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 66 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The massacre at Jallianwala Bagh in Amritsar on 13 April 1919 is the event that has stayed in memory. A) Tj T* (gathering that had been prohibited was fired upon by troops under General Dyer, and the Hunter) Tj T* (Committee that examined this event did not produce accountability proportionate to the loss of life. The) Tj T* (lesson drawn by the nationalist movement was not only that force had been excessive, but that the law had) Tj T* (given executive officers an almost unreviewable discretion over whether a crowd was lawful.) Tj T* ET
