BT 1 0 0 1 0 81.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The freedom movement turned assembly into a political method. The Non-Cooperation Movement, the Salt) Tj T* (Satyagraha of 1930 and the Quit India movement of 1942 were all, in different ways, deliberate) Tj T* (confrontations with prohibitory orders. The Congress resolution on Fundamental Rights adopted at Karachi) Tj T* (in 1931 listed freedom of speech, association and assembly among the rights a free India would guarantee,) Tj T* (and these demands travelled into the Constituent Assembly. The claim that was being made was a structural) Tj T* (one: that assembly is a right the State must justify restricting, not a favour the State may withdraw.) Tj T* ET
