BT 1 0 0 1 0 174.5 Tm 15.5 TL 1 1 1 rg /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (India has had a long standing history with student-led movements. Student movements have challenged) Tj T* (colonial rule, corruption, discrimination, and even basic rights. Student campaigns have widened democratic) Tj T* (participation and brought together young minds from different castes, classes, and belonging. One of the) Tj T* (first instances of student demonstrations ranges back to the Swadeshi Movement following Bengal\001s) Tj T* (partition in 1905 where students joined boycotts. As a result, the British began to expel students from) Tj T* (schools and threatened further consequences. To support such students, Sachindraprasad Basu formed the) Tj T* (Anti-Circular Society, which helped arrange alternative education. Historian Sumit Sarkar\001s account shows) Tj T* (that student organisers were active participants in building these alternatives, rather than simply following) Tj T* (established nationalist leaders. Even during the Non-cooperation Movement \(1920-1922\), students rejected) Tj T* (schools and colleges, stating that participation in such colonial institutions helped sustain the authority they) Tj T* (opposed. At Osmania University in 1938, students defied restrictions on singing ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Vande Mataram) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL ( under the) Tj T* (Nizam\001s administration.) Tj T* ET
