BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The right to peaceful protest in India is not derived from a single constitutional provision. It emerges from) Tj T* (the relationship between the freedoms of speech and expression, peaceful assembly, personal liberty and) Tj T* (the constitutional limits placed upon the exercise of State power. The Constitution recognises that citizens) Tj T* (must be able to express disagreement with the government and assemble to pursue common political or) Tj T* -0.022754 Tw (social objectives. At the same time, it permits the State to impose reasonable restrictions where the exercise) Tj T* 0 Tw (of these rights threatens public order or other constitutionally protected interests. The central question for) Tj T* (this agenda is therefore not whether the State may regulate protest, but the extent to which such regulation) Tj T* (can be justified without undermining the rights it is required to protect.) Tj T* ET
