q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.5 Tm 15.5 TL 1 1 1 rg /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The phrase carries much of the weight in this agenda, and the Supreme Court has been careful about its) Tj T* -0.000644 Tw (meaning. In ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Ram Manohar Lohia v. State of Bihar) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL ( \(1966\) the Court distinguished three concentric circles: law) Tj T* 0 Tw (and order, public order and the security of the State, with disturbance of the first not necessarily amounting) Tj T* (to disturbance of the second. In ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Arun Ghosh v. State of West Bengal) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL ( \(1970\) Justice Hidayatullah explained) Tj T* (that the question is whether an act disturbs the even tempo of the life of the community, as opposed to a) Tj T* (few individuals. The consequence for this agenda is significant. A Section 163 order grounded on mere) Tj T* -0.005206 Tw (inconvenience, or on an ordinary law and order problem, does not satisfy the constitutional ground of public) Tj T* 0 Tw (order unless the apprehended disturbance reaches the community more broadly.) Tj T* ET
