BT 1 0 0 1 0 190 Tm 15.5 TL 1 1 1 rg /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Article 19 requires restrictions to be "reasonable", and the courts treat this as a requirement with both) Tj T* (substantive and procedural content. In ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (State of Madras v. V.G. Row) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL ( \(1952\) the Supreme Court said that the) Tj T* (test of reasonableness looks at the nature of the right, the purpose of the restriction, its extent and urgency) Tj T* (and the disproportion between the imposition and the mischief it addresses. The Court has more recently) Tj T* (moved to a structured proportionality analysis, set out in ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Modern Dental College v. State of Madhya Pradesh) Tj  T* /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (\(2016\) and developed in the privacy and Aadhaar judgments, and the Court applied it to restrictions on) Tj T* (communication in ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Anuradha Bhasin) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (. In the form generally used, the test asks whether the restriction) Tj T* (pursues a legitimate aim, whether there is a rational connection between the restriction and that aim,) Tj T* (whether there is a less restrictive alternative that would achieve the aim equally well, and whether the) Tj T* (benefit to the aim outweighs the harm to the right. The necessity limb is where most protest cases will be) Tj T* (decided. A district-wide prohibition on all gatherings of five or more persons must be justified against) Tj T* (narrower options such as designated routes, crowd caps, time limits or targeted orders against specific) Tj T* (persons.) Tj T* ET
