BT 1 0 0 1 0 153.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15 TL (For the purposes of this agenda the most important fact about the BNSS is how much of the CrPC it carries) Tj T* -0.104876 Tw (over. The urgent-orders power of Section 144 was re-enacted as Section 163 with its grounds, duration limits) Tj T* 0 Tw (and ex parte mechanism essentially unchanged. The dispersal provisions, the power to arrest to prevent a) Tj T* (cognisable offence and the power to require security for keeping the peace were also carried over with new) Tj T* (numbers. The Supreme Court has itself treated the new provision as pari materia with the old one. What the) Tj T* (BNSS added, in the field of public order, is Section 172, which has no direct counterpart in the old Code, and) Tj T* (the restructured rules on custody and remand. The scope of Section 172 therefore depends substantially on) Tj T* (the meaning of \002lawful directions,\003 the duties contemplated by Chapter XII, and the circumstances in which) Tj T* (non-compliance may justify detention or removal. Delegates should therefore be wary of arguments that) Tj T* -0.031775 Tw (attribute the whole of the present controversy to the new Sanhita. A good deal of it is the old power, used in) Tj T* 0 Tw (a new setting.) Tj T* ET
