BT 1 0 0 1 0 198.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15 TL (Several questions are unresolved and should be on the floor of the committee. How should "apprehended) Tj T* (danger" be understood, and does it require a specific and imminent threat, or is a general anticipation of) Tj T* (disorder enough? When a Section 163 order covers a whole district and bans every assembly of five or more) Tj T* (persons, is that proportionate, given that the text allows an order addressed to the public generally? What is) Tj T* -0.048419 Tw (the legal status of an exemption in the order itself, for instance one that allows assembly at a designated site) Tj T* 0 Tw (only with prior written permission, and does such a clause convert a prohibitory order into a licensing) Tj T* (regime? Does presence at a gathering in breach of a prohibitory order, without any further wrongful act,) Tj T* (make an assembly unlawful under the BNS, or does that depend on the common object of the assembly?) Tj T* (Judicial opinion and police practice on this last point have not been uniform. And finally, where) Tj T* (administrative steps such as the suspension of Metro services, the cancellation of trains or the restriction of) Tj T* (mobile internet are taken in connection with an assembly, they rest on different legal bases, including) Tj T* (powers of the railway and Metro authorities and rules under the Telecommunications Act, 2023, rather than) Tj T* (on the BNSS. Whether Parliament should require those steps to meet the same standards as a Section 163) Tj T* (order is a separate legislative question.) Tj T* ET
