BT 1 0 0 1 0 128 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The protests surrounding the Special Intensive Revision \(SIR\) of electoral rolls in October 2026 brought the) Tj T* (constitutional debate over peaceful assembly and preventive policing into sharp focus. The demonstrations,) Tj T* (organised by the Cockroach Janta Party and associated youth activists, called for the resignation of Chief) Tj T* (Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. Protesters raised concerns regarding the revision of electoral rolls) Tj T* (and the potential exclusion of eligible voters. The Election Commission and the government, however,) Tj T* (maintained that the revision process was intended to remove entries relating to deceased, relocated or) Tj T* (otherwise ineligible individuals. The controversy therefore extended beyond the conduct of the protests) Tj T* (themselves, involving questions concerning electoral integrity, political accountability and the right of) Tj T* (citizens to collectively express their grievances.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 44 441.3898 cm
q
1 1 1 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Ahead of the demonstrations, authorities in Delhi imposed prohibitory restrictions under Section 163 of the) Tj T* (Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023, and undertook extensive security measures in central parts of the) Tj T* (capital. These included the deployment of police and paramilitary personnel, restrictions around Jantar) Tj T* (Mantar, the closure of several Metro stations, the suspension of certain railway services and restrictions on) Tj T* (internet connectivity. The stated objective of the authorities was to prevent disorder and maintain public) Tj T* (safety in an area containing important government institutions and public infrastructure. Protesters and) Tj T* (opposition representatives, however, questioned the geographical extent of the restrictions and whether) Tj T* (the measures imposed were necessary to address the anticipated threat.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 44 310.3898 cm
q
1 1 1 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (On 10 October 2026, large numbers of protesters were detained as the authorities sought to prevent the) Tj T* (gathering from proceeding. Reports concerning the scale of detention varied considerably. Reuters reported) Tj T* (that more than 2,000 protesters had been detained in Delhi, while proceedings before the Supreme Court) Tj T* (subsequently referred to allegations involving approximately 7,000 individuals. The government disputed) Tj T* (allegations of widespread illegal detention and stated that the persons referred to in the proceedings had) Tj T* -0.121371 Tw (been released. These differing accounts are important to the legal assessment of the incident, as the number) Tj T* 0 Tw (of persons detained, the grounds for each detention and the geographical area within which the detentions) Tj T* (occurred remain relevant to determining whether the police action was lawful.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 44 163.8898 cm
q
1 1 1 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 128 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The restrictions also raised questions concerning the relationship between protest regulation and the rights) Tj T* (of the wider public. The closure of Metro stations and disruption of railway services affected not only those) Tj T* (participating in the demonstrations, but also ordinary commuters attempting to travel through the capital.) Tj T* (While authorities may regulate transport facilities where a genuine threat to public order exists, the) Tj T* (complete or extensive suspension of essential services requires a separate justification. The legality of such) Tj T* (measures cannot be assumed merely because they were undertaken in connection with a protest. Metro) Tj T* (services, railway operations and internet restrictions are governed by legal frameworks distinct from Section) Tj T* (163 of the BNSS, and their validity must be assessed under the relevant statutory provisions and) Tj T* (constitutional standards.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 44 79.3898 cm
q
1 1 1 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 66 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The Supreme Court intervened on 9 and 11 October 2026 in proceedings concerning the restrictions and) Tj T* (alleged detentions. On 9 October, the Court expressed concern regarding the complete prohibition of) Tj T* (essential public transportation and emphasised that the operation of Metro and railway services could be) Tj T* (regulated in a proportionate manner rather than prohibited outright. The authorities were also directed to) Tj T* (consider suitable alternative sites for peaceful demonstrations and to issue public traffic advisories.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 44 41.3898 cm
q
1 1 1 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 19.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (On 11 October, the Court convened an urgent hearing in response to allegations that its earlier directions) Tj T* (had not been complied with and that protesters had been subjected to unlawful detention. The Court) Tj T* ET
