1 1 1 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (The Anti-SIR protests raise several questions central to this agenda. First, whether a prohibitory order) Tj T* (covering a broad geographical area can be justified by apprehended disorder associated with a particular) Tj T* (gathering, or whether the authorities must demonstrate why narrower restrictions would be insufficient.) Tj T* (Second, whether detentions undertaken to prevent an assembly from proceeding satisfy the requirements) Tj T* (of Sections 170 and 172 of the BNSS, particularly where individuals are not alleged to have committed any) Tj T* (independent offence. Third, whether restrictions upon Metro, railway and internet services may be justified) Tj T* (by the same apprehension of danger that supports a Section 163 order, or whether each measure requires) Tj T* (an independent assessment of necessity and proportionality.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
