BT 1 0 0 1 0 221 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Given the legal and contemporary nature of the agenda, the Executive Board has decided not to provide) Tj T* (delegates with a prescribed list of research papers, articles, or external links delegates are encouraged to) Tj T* (develop their own legal interpretations and political positions, rather than rely on a prescribed set of) Tj T* (sources. Since the subject involves evolving jurisprudence, ongoing political developments and competing) Tj T* (interpretations of the law, providing a fixed reading list could unnecessarily limit the scope of research or) Tj T* (privilege particular perspectives. The delegates can undertake independent research into the constitutional,) Tj T* (statutory, and judicial dimensions of the right to peaceful protest in India. Particular emphasis should be) Tj T* (placed on the interpretation and application of relevant provisions of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha) Tj T* -0.007409 Tw (Sanhita, 2023, landmark judicial precedents concerning public assemblies, and the evolving jurisprudence on) Tj T* 0 Tw (the balance between individual liberties and public order. Delegates should also examine recent) Tj T* (developments in the National Capital Territory of Delhi, the role of executive and police authorities in) Tj T* (regulating demonstrations, and the institutional complexities surrounding the administration of public order) Tj T* (in Delhi. A thorough understanding of these issues, alongside the positions of the ruling government and) Tj T* (opposition, will enable delegates to engage in informed parliamentary deliberation and formulate legally) Tj T* (sound, viable, and consistent solutions.) Tj T* ET
